                <pb facs="0975" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">637.0023/46: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Howell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-23T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>78. Colonel Tarafa has conferred with the Department, but the Department has not
                    invited the representatives of other railway systems to make statements.</p>
                <p>The Department understands that there will be conference between Tarafa and sugar
                    interests to discuss the proposal to eliminate from the bill the provisions
                    closing existing private ports but to retain the provisions prohibiting imports
                    through private ports, and to add a provision prohibiting in the future the
                    establishment of private ports.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
